# CLI

Every entry node includes an interactive command-line interface for direct access to the node state. The CLI is automatically disabled when stdin is not a terminal (e.g., in Docker or when running as a daemon).

## Commands

| Command | Aliases | Description |
|---------|---------|-------------|
| `ping` | `p` | Show version and uptime |
| `stats` | `s` | Show traffic statistics |
| `peers` | - | List connected peers and sessions |
| `route add <cidr> via <peer_id>` | - | Add a route |
| `route del <cidr>` | - | Remove a route |
| `route list` | `routes`, `ip route` | List all routes |
| `disconnect <peer_id>` | - | Disconnect a peer |
| `help` | `?` | Show this help message |
| `quit` | `q` | Exit wallhack |

## Example Session

```
wallhack> stats
Traffic Statistics:
  Bytes In:     1.23 MB
  Bytes Out:    456.78 KB

wallhack> route add 10.0.0.0/8 via peer1
Route added: 10.0.0.0/8
```
